<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Three entitlements, and the list is meant to stay this short.

	§6.5 was "no network" without qualification until 2026-08-14, and its absence
	from this file was what made that enforceable by the OS rather than by
	discipline. The owner amended it to allow one destination — a QRZ callsign
	lookup on his own subscription (§10.4) — and network.client below is what that
	cost. It cannot be taken back while this key is here.

	What survives the amendment, and what this file still enforces:

	  * com.apple.security.network.server must NEVER appear here. The app listens
	    for nothing. That half of the original rule is untouched.

	  * network.client is for QRZ's XML service and nothing else. Any second
	    destination — an update check, a callsign database, a POTA API, telemetry
	    of any kind — is a new decision needing the same conversation decision 17
	    records, not a free ride on this key.

	user-selected.read-write is the sandbox's file access: the user picks a file in
	the open panel, and that grant covers it. Writing the split's output files (§10.2)
	is covered by the destination folder the user chooses.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
